+raised. Rules are compared based on their path, subdomain or host, websocket
+mode, and methods. Rules are duplicates if they share any method, since only the
+first rule would ever match requests using that method. A rule that doesn't
+specify ``methods`` allows any method, so it overlaps with every other rule for
+the same path. Variable parts are not equal if they use different converters,
+although this heuristic may not be perfect depending on what the different
+converters can actually match.
 
 
